// This program implements a sorting algorithm that can be evolved to adapt to different data patterns



// EVOLVE-BLOCK-START
// HYPOTHESIS-1: Switching to sort_unstable_by with a comparator that falls back to stable tie-break by original index for equal keys will improve adaptability_score on duplicate-heavy inputs while staying fast.
// MECHANISM-1: Comparator-induced total ordering prevents pathological partitioning behavior for many equal elements and reduces run-to-run variance.
// EXPECT-1: adaptability_score > 0.9998
